    "answer": {
      "short": "Repetitions are not counted in sets, so Mary is correct.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A\\cup B&=\\{1,2,3,4,5\\}\\\\|A\\cup B|&=5.\\end{align*}$$\nMary is correct. Each distinct element is counted once; Bob has counted the common elements $1$, $2$ and $3$ twice.",
